---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const experience = [
  {
    title: 'FPGA / Firmware Engineering Intern',
    org: 'Indra, Air Defence',
    period: 'Apr 2026 – Aug 2026',
    place: 'Torrejón de Ardoz (Madrid), Spain',
    points: [
      "Ported a senior engineer's Cyclone IV prototype of a fixed-point down-conversion chain to a Xilinx Artix-7 200T in VHDL and re-architected it for 416 MHz: 99-tap complex FIR, NCO mixer and decimate-by-13 polyphase filter.",
      "Closed timing at 416 MHz (2.4 ns period) by hand-instantiating DSP48E1 cascades where Vivado's inference left the delay line in fabric, moving lookup tables into registered block RAM, re-pipelining critical paths and floorplanning with Pblocks.",
      'Built a fixed-point MATLAB reference model and validated each RTL stage against it by dumping testbench outputs to CSV and comparing the sequences in MATLAB.',
      'Wrote an SPI master and control state machines to bring up a TI high-speed ADC (44 registers written and read back); debugged on the board with an integrated logic analyser and oscilloscope.',
    ],
    link: { label: 'Project pages', href: url('/projects/fpga-ddc-416mhz') },
  },
  {
    title: 'Electrical Engineering Intern',
    org: 'Valladares Ingeniería',
    period: 'Nov 2025 – Mar 2026',
    place: 'Madrid, Spain',
    points: ['Design and on-site follow-up of electrical installations for construction projects, working with the other engineering areas.'],
  },
  {
    title: 'Private tutor',
    org: 'Self-employed',
    period: 'Sep 2021 – Jul 2025',
    place: 'Madrid, Spain',
    points: ['Maths and science for high-school and university students, including university entrance exam preparation.'],
  },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Career development"
  eyebrow="Career"
  description="Experience and career goals of Nicolás Izquierdo Arruga: FPGA internship at Indra, looking for a hardware engineering internship (FPGA-focused) in summer 2027."
  lead={`${SITE.focus} The MSc requires an internship in summer 2027.`}
>
  <h2>Paths I find interesting</h2>
  <p>
    FPGA design is my focus, but I also like the rest of the board: analog front ends, ADCs, firmware and the lab work to make them run together. Two paths
    interest me most.
  </p>

  <h3>Space and defence</h3>
  <p>
    I want to work on real space hardware, especially FPGAs, in environments where a design has to keep working when
    things go wrong. My internship at Indra showed me what FPGA work for defence looks like, and I would like to keep
    going in that direction. My MSc track (Aeronautics and Space) and the{' '}
    <a href={url('/projects/astreloon')}>AstreLoon balloon</a> point the same way. The space industry is also growing
    fast in Spain and the rest of Europe, with many new start-ups.
  </p>
  <p>Projects I would like to be part of:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>SoCs that combine FPGAs and processors for signal processing.</li>
    <li>AI workloads running on board, on FPGAs and embedded systems.</li>
    <li>AI applied to HDL design and verification.</li>
    <li>Optoelectronics.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    I would most like to work in a lab, closer to research than to production, where I can prototype, test and debug
    my own designs on real hardware.
  </p>

  <h3>High-frequency trading</h3>
  <p>
    Finance has interested me for a long time. Only recently did I find out how much these firms rely on hardware
    engineers, with FPGAs that react to the market in nanoseconds. A role there would bring together two things I
    am interested in. The focus on latency also connects with my FPGA work at Indra, where closing timing at 416 MHz
    was the main challenge.
  </p>
  <p>Projects I would like to be part of:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Low-latency market-data handling on FPGAs, such as parsing exchange feeds. My{' '}
      <a href={url('/projects/itch-parser')}>ITCH feed handler</a> is a first step in that direction.
    </li>
    <li>Network packet processing in hardware.</li>
    <li>Verification of these designs, so they are fast and also correct.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Both paths share what I enjoy most: fast, reliable digital hardware, tested on real boards.
  </p>

  <h2>Experience</h2>
  <Timeline items={experience} />

  <h2>CV</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={url('/cv')}>Download my CV</a> (one-page PDF).
  </p>
</PageLayout>
